Chapter: SerialLineTest

  cites Foreword chapter SerialLine

 Exercise the serial-line HAL: RS485 half-duplex direction discipline,
 RS232 full-duplex freedom, and the linear bus grant. Each scenario
 returns a packed integer (tx * 100 + rx * 10 + faults) so one check
 verifies transmit accounting, receive accounting, and fault counting
 together. opening returns the count of passing checks.

Section: Scenarios

 RS485 half-duplex: the first transmit happens while receiving (a
 fault, no bytes sent); after enabling the driver two transmits send
 5 bytes; a receive while driving is a fault; after disabling the
 driver a receive takes 4 bytes. Expect tx=5, rx=4, faults=2 -> 542.

  rs485-scenario : Integer
  rs485-scenario =
   let p0 = serial-open rs485-half-config
   in let p1 = serial-transmit p0 [1, 2, 3]
   in let p2 = serial-drive-enable p1
   in let p3 = serial-transmit p2 [1, 2, 3]
   in let p4 = serial-transmit p3 [4, 5]
   in let p5 = serial-receive p4 4
   in let p6 = serial-drive-disable p5
   in let p7 = serial-receive p6 4
   in serial-tx-bytes p7 * 100 + serial-rx-bytes p7 * 10 + serial-faults p7

 RS232 is full-duplex: transmit and receive are always allowed
 regardless of direction. Expect tx=2, rx=3, faults=0 -> 230.

  rs232-scenario : Integer
  rs232-scenario =
   let p0 = serial-open rs232-config
   in let p1 = serial-transmit p0 [1, 2]
   in let p2 = serial-receive p1 3
   in serial-tx-bytes p2 * 100 + serial-rx-bytes p2 * 10 + serial-faults p2

 RS485 full-duplex (four-wire) also imposes no direction constraint:
 a transmit while still in receive succeeds. Expect tx=3.

  rs485-full-scenario : Integer
  rs485-full-scenario =
   let p0 = serial-open rs485-full-config
   in let p1 = serial-transmit p0 [1, 2, 3]
   in serial-tx-bytes p1

 Direction control: after enabling the driver the direction code is 1.

  dir-scenario : Integer
  dir-scenario =
   let p0 = serial-open rs485-half-config
   in let p1 = serial-drive-enable p0
   in serial-direction-code p1

 Linear bus grant: acquire, thread through two transmits, release
 exactly once. The node id (7) survives the round trip.

  bus-scenario : Integer
  bus-scenario =
   let g0 = serial-bus-acquire 7
   in let g1 = serial-bus-transmit g0 [1, 2, 3]
   in let g2 = serial-bus-transmit g1 [4, 5]
   in serial-bus-release g2

Section: Checks

  flag : Boolean -> Integer
  flag (b) = if b then 1 else 0

  opening : Integer =
   let a = flag (rs485-scenario == 542)
   in let b = flag (rs232-scenario == 230)
   in let c = flag (rs485-full-scenario == 3)
   in let d = flag (dir-scenario == 1)
   in let e = flag (bus-scenario == 7)
   in a + b + c + d + e
